e protected Racket runtime agreed with\nthe expected output on all five, and the rival disagreed only on the generated\nwitness. Exact rule SHA-256: `c83accbef454499a8c9af94eaf34ddd2d50551e7312ed9a0360c34a00985fd89`.\n\nThe generator emits this exact witness under the request above. Its default\nfour-slot schedule contains two incomplete and two complete orientation sets in\neach difficulty band, so every three-demonstration holdout contains at least one\ncase that refutes this rival. The retained 300-lesson census found zero ambiguity\nin 1,200 query rotations; this is finite declared-rival evidence, not universal\nidentifiability proof.\n","verification_status":"reviewer_reported"}
